Switch: throttle the warm-up only after a slow build (aurora_switch_set_warmup_slow_ns)

With Mesa's persistent shader cache a warm-up build costs 11-13 ms when the cache has the shaders
and 100-300 ms when it does not. Patch 0009 idled the compile thread after every warm-up build
for (1 - duty) / duty of its duration and then waited for a present, so a warm cache still
warmed up at about one pipeline per frame (~1098 pipelines in a minute or more) instead of back
to back (~6 s). Now only a build longer than the slow threshold (default 25 ms, about a frame:
a cache miss) holds the next one back; after a fast one the next starts at once. The threshold is
set with aurora_switch_set_warmup_slow_ns (0: every build held back, as before);
aurora_switch_get_precompile reports the builds that were not held back (unthrottled).

Switch only (switch/native/aurora/patches); not for upstream.

